Source: snd-zg01-dkms
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Brice Sauvajon <brice@sauvajon.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.0
Homepage: https://github.com/bsauvajon/snd-zg01

Package: snd-zg01-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 2.1.0.0), alsa-ucm-conf
Description: DKMS driver for Yamaha ZG01 USB audio interface
 This package provides the snd-zg01 kernel module for the Yamaha ZG01
 USB audio interface (VID: 0x0499, PID: 0x1513).
 .
 Features:
  - Game Channel (Output): Crystal-clear 32-bit stereo playback
  - Voice Channel (Input): Low-latency microphone capture
  - Full-duplex support for simultaneous playback and capture
  - 48kHz sample rate, S32_LE format
  - Perfect audio quality with no clicks or sample skipping
 .
 The module will be automatically rebuilt for new kernel versions
 using DKMS (Dynamic Kernel Module Support).

Package: snd-zg01-tools
Section: sound
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: snd-zg01-dkms
Description: Control CLI for the Yamaha ZG01 driver
 zgctl lists and sets the Yamaha ZG01 mic DSP controls exposed by the
 snd-zg01 driver: the GATE, compressor, equalizer and limiter, plus
 saving and reloading the device settings.  It talks to the ALSA control
 device directly and needs no libasound.
 .
 This package is architecture dependent (it ships a compiled binary);
 the snd-zg01-dkms package stays architecture independent.
